 concept:'Summarising data: measures of location (mean, median, mode) and spread (range, IQR, variance, standard deviation), including from grouped data by interpolation and from coded data. Representing it: histograms (where area, not height, is frequency), box plots and the outlier rule, cumulative frequency, and scatter diagrams with correlation and regression. The exam rewards interpretation in context as much as calculation — "strong negative correlation between temperature and heating cost" scores where "r = −0.85" alone does not. Your calculator does the arithmetic; your job is to set it up correctly and say what the number means.',
